# What must not reach the build context.
#
# Two rules, and the second is the one that costs real money when forgotten: nothing enormous, and
# nothing secret. An image built here is pushed to a *public* Docker Hub repository, so anything in
# this directory that is not excluded below is published to the world.

# Regenerated inside the image by `next build`.
node_modules
.next/
out/

# History and local tooling: no use at runtime.
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets. `.env*.local` is gitignored, which is exactly why it would otherwise still be here.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# The live content. It is mounted at runtime from the host, never baked in — the image ships only
# `content.default`, so the same public image serves the demo for anyone who runs it and the real
# site for the host that has a volume. Leaving it out is what keeps those two facts independent.
content/

# Deployment descriptors for the other host, and a load-test script.
amplify.yml
customHttp.yml
test_speed.py
